counterfactuals.output:
**Claim 1.** A method for fabricating a metal component having a hole, the method comprising:

depositing a first release layer comprising a dispersed ceramic powder onto a build surface;

forming a first support structure of model material over the first release layer;

depositing a second release layer comprising a dispersed ceramic powder over the first support structure at a location corresponding to the hole to be formed in the metal component;

depositing a model material defining the metal component over the second release layer and the first support structure such that the second release layer is disposed within the deposited model material at the location of the hole;

heating the deposited model material to sinter the model material into the metal component while the first and second release layers of dispersed ceramic powder remain unsintered; and

removing the first support structure and the unsintered first and second release layers from the metal component, thereby releasing the metal component from the build surface and forming the hole at the location of the second release layer.
